1
00:00:45,250 --> 00:01:44,710
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:06,860
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION.

3
00:02:56,470 --> 00:02:59,920
Look at the trouble we're going through
to make that foul creature live.

4
00:03:00,770 --> 00:03:03,150
Cruel world.

5
00:03:11,890 --> 00:03:14,370
I forged the steel thoroughly, Batur Bey.

6
00:03:14,370 --> 00:03:18,370
No one in this world can defeat you now.

7
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:21,450
If it lets me down during a battle...

8
00:03:23,370 --> 00:03:27,560
... then no one can save you from
me, blacksmith.

9
00:03:48,710 --> 00:03:51,910
I wonder what you're up to now.

10
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:16,780
All of them were lies.

11
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:19,000
Kalonoz.

12
00:04:19,430 --> 00:04:22,790
- Listen to me.
- God damn you.

13
00:04:28,970 --> 00:04:30,420
Stop!

14
00:04:31,630 --> 00:04:33,570
Who are you?

15
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:26,500
We are the only force that will get
Byzantine back on its feet.

16
00:05:27,090 --> 00:05:29,110
Commander Kalonoz.

17
00:05:34,190 --> 00:05:39,130
We're the only masters of that
great, holy power.

18
00:05:41,890 --> 00:05:45,890
We swore to fight the Turks and bring our
empire to its former glory...

19
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:53,290
... and protect Hagia Sophia in
Constantinople.

20
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:56,630
Who are you?

21
00:05:56,630 --> 00:06:00,630
Yannis. Monk Yannis.

22
00:06:02,230 --> 00:06:07,010
I'm a loyal servant of the Margaret
Church in Serres.

23
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:14,750
Everyone you see here, in the name of
our church, are guards of Kulucahisar.

24
00:06:23,410 --> 00:06:28,280
Kulucahisar is just one of the castles
under our control.

25
00:06:29,030 --> 00:06:35,440
Many more castles, with their commanders,
soldiers, and even governors...

26
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:37,480
... are under our control.

27
00:06:38,970 --> 00:06:40,670
Sofia.

28
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:43,420
What about you?

29
00:06:43,870 --> 00:06:46,940
Growing with the hate of the Turkish...

30
00:06:48,250 --> 00:06:52,260
... I'm a woman who has always
obeyed Master Yannis.

31
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:02,070
I'm a woman who couldn't tell her
feelings...

32
00:07:02,610 --> 00:07:06,300
... to the man she loved, because
of this cause.

33
00:07:09,550 --> 00:07:13,550
I offer a commander like you to
join us....

34
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:21,810
... to become more powerful, and to
fight the Turks until the end...

35
00:07:21,810 --> 00:07:23,850
... Commander Kalonoz.

36
00:07:45,470 --> 00:07:46,840
Tell me.

37
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:49,660
What were you looking for in the castle?

38
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:52,240
It's obvious that you took
something hidden.

39
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:55,370
Was it, the treasure?

40
00:07:55,860 --> 00:07:59,650
You're right, Osman. It was the treasure.

41
00:07:59,650 --> 00:08:03,930
But we neither stole nor seized it.

42
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:09,790
With the help and grace of Allah, we
took back what was ours.

43
00:08:11,250 --> 00:08:14,890
That treasure in its entirety, belongs
to the Ahis.

44
00:08:14,890 --> 00:08:18,890
I know Ahis, and how they
withstand to Mongolians.

45
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:22,660
But I'm uncomfortable, Edebali.

46
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:27,470
Why are the ones in the castle opposed
you? Why did they steal your treasure?

47
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:30,310
What happened in the castle?

48
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:35,890
Your daughter Bala, Father Tursun, why
were they there?

49
00:08:36,740 --> 00:08:43,230
A dark force ruling Bithynia has spread
everywhere, every corner.

50
00:08:43,710 --> 00:08:47,710
Sometimes they dominate with their
ideas...

51
00:08:47,710 --> 00:08:51,350
... and sometimes with the men they pick.

52
00:08:51,350 --> 00:08:55,350
What do they want? What are they after?

53
00:08:55,760 --> 00:09:02,470
They want to end our beliefs with
the darkness they laid upon us, son.

54
00:09:03,860 --> 00:09:10,140
They want to kick the Turks out of
these lands and revive Byzantine's spirit.

55
00:09:12,210 --> 00:09:15,380
They know Ahis won't surrender.

56
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:22,100
To be ahead of us, they stole the
treasure that is Ahis' fortune.

57
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:27,670
They want to push us into an
economic crisis, son.

58
00:09:32,850 --> 00:09:37,250
Even Sofia who killed the governor and
captured the castle...

59
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:39,590
... is their agent in the castle.

60
00:09:41,630 --> 00:09:45,990
The ones who stole this treasure from
you, as you described...

61
00:09:45,990 --> 00:09:48,780
... a dark and great power, Edebali.

62
00:09:48,780 --> 00:09:55,280
The force behind the ones who believe in
Allah, is always greater, son.

63
00:09:56,410 --> 00:10:00,410
We neither have concerns, nor fears.

64
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:06,540
We know and believe that no matter how
angry the enemy's armies are...

65
00:10:07,350 --> 00:10:11,350
... there is a Mount Hira for every
truth.

66
00:10:15,970 --> 00:10:18,310
The things you've told me cheered me up.

67
00:10:18,950 --> 00:10:23,650
I have a strong feeling that, during
all this trouble...

68
00:10:24,170 --> 00:10:27,210
... what we need is a strong union.

69
00:10:27,550 --> 00:10:32,980
A majestic union no enemy can weaken.

70
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:37,090
Maybe...

71
00:10:38,570 --> 00:10:41,770
... maybe even a state.

72
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:49,290
This shall be such a state that with
it, justice should be revived.

73
00:10:49,830 --> 00:10:52,560
Islamic world shall find peace.

74
00:10:53,100 --> 00:11:00,590
The cruel shall shake, manners shall rise
up with it.

75
00:11:06,210 --> 00:11:10,490
Don't be surprised, Commander Kalonoz.
Just answer.

76
00:11:11,300 --> 00:11:13,190
Are you with us?

77
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:26,420
Let's say I'm not.

78
00:11:30,260 --> 00:11:32,280
Will kill me too?

79
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:39,450
No commander who has no hatred for the
Turkish, has the right to live, Kalonoz.

80
00:11:41,870 --> 00:11:44,460
We set off for a great cause.

81
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:47,350
And our enemies are so close that...

82
00:11:47,350 --> 00:11:52,320
... there is absolutely no room in
our hearts for mercy.

83
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:54,450
Who are those enemies?

84
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:57,470
Sheikh Edebali, and his Ahis.

85
00:11:58,680 --> 00:12:01,980
An old Sheikh, and a handful of Ahis.

86
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:06,100
Why do they bother you so
much, Monk Yannis?

87
00:12:08,010 --> 00:12:10,530
You don't know them, Kalonoz.

88
00:12:12,430 --> 00:12:17,110
Sheikh Edebali is the soul of the Turkish
who cannot be captured.

89
00:12:18,790 --> 00:12:22,010
Even the Mongolians
couldn't deal with Ahis.

90
00:12:22,010 --> 00:12:27,420
The moment we think they are done
with, they will start a new beginning.

91
00:12:27,570 --> 00:12:31,330
Then, how will you deal with them?

92
00:12:31,750 --> 00:12:36,900
With heroes like you, who kill and die
for their causes.

93
00:12:38,270 --> 00:12:41,790
We Greeks, have an ancient saying.

94
00:12:42,290 --> 00:12:46,460
If you're going to hunt wolfs, sharpen
your axe.

95
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:52,600
If we don't sharpen our axes, we can't
oppose the Turkish.

96
00:12:53,550 --> 00:12:57,550
And if we can't oppose them, Sheikh
Edebali and his Ahis...

97
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:03,770
... will unite with Ghazis (Veterans),
Alps (Men), Bacıyans (Women)...

98
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:07,060
... and that will be our doom.

99
00:13:08,430 --> 00:13:13,560
Now I will ask again, Commander Kalonoz.

100
00:13:15,490 --> 00:13:19,490
After many years, do you want to be
remembered as a traitor...

101
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:24,740
... or as a hero who stopped the
Turks' rush?

102
00:13:46,090 --> 00:13:50,090
In this holy journey,
I'm with you until my death.

103
00:15:35,550 --> 00:15:37,480
Shut your mouth. Shut up!

104
00:16:06,300 --> 00:16:08,090
Shut up!

105
00:16:13,810 --> 00:16:16,920
Only if my Osman Bey didn't need you...

106
00:16:17,950 --> 00:16:20,530
... so I could skin you alive.

107
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:50,420
I told you everything I knew. Let me go!

108
00:16:50,420 --> 00:16:52,260
Shut up. Shut up!

109
00:17:04,330 --> 00:17:08,210
Open it, open it!

110
00:17:56,630 --> 00:17:59,450
Now sit here quietly.

111
00:19:26,710 --> 00:19:30,040
One question, one answer.

112
00:19:30,680 --> 00:19:32,710
Who are you?

113
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:13,020
- Peace be with you.
- Friends.

114
00:20:13,270 --> 00:20:15,320
Peace be with you too.

115
00:20:37,210 --> 00:20:41,070
Separate the double and single-threaded
ones well.

116
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:45,290
The ones with patterns are still
incomplete.

117
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:48,250
We can't sell them like this in the
bazaar.

118
00:20:48,250 --> 00:20:50,990
- Very well, Bala Hatun.
- Very well, Bala Hatun.

119
00:21:05,830 --> 00:21:08,920
These ones are not suitable for selling.

120
00:21:09,530 --> 00:21:12,410
Turn them into boots for the unfortunate
and give them away.

121
00:21:12,410 --> 00:21:14,340
Very well, Bala Hatun.

122
00:21:26,490 --> 00:21:31,730
Not only in swinging swords, but you're
also skilled in trading, Bala Hatun.

123
00:21:32,090 --> 00:21:35,530
We can protect our lives with swords,
Turks' dignity with trade...

124
00:21:35,530 --> 00:21:38,050
... and traditions with our manners,
Osman Bey.

125
00:21:39,100 --> 00:21:44,050
The Turkish's traditions are on women's
hands, my dear mother used to say.

126
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:49,140
Thanks to you, I realised how right
she was.

127
00:21:53,950 --> 00:21:55,750
Bala Hatun.

128
00:21:56,180 --> 00:21:58,930
- Your horse Alaca.
- What happened to Alaca?

129
00:21:58,930 --> 00:22:02,480
The situation is not good in the barn.

130
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:41,680
No grass can grow in your path, my friend.

131
00:22:42,460 --> 00:22:45,510
Bala Hatun's wing, my Alaca.

132
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:51,140
I'd never known I'd see you like this.

133
00:22:58,580 --> 00:23:02,200
He jumped right out of the Epic of Manas
to my life, Osman Bey.

134
00:23:11,480 --> 00:23:14,830
He was my guide.

135
00:23:16,630 --> 00:23:22,470
Like the moon in the sky, My Alaca was my
crescent with its light in the dark.

136
00:23:29,650 --> 00:23:31,670
My Alaca.

137
00:23:31,910 --> 00:23:33,970
Excuse him, Bala Hatun.

138
00:23:34,510 --> 00:23:38,510
How can you be mad at the moon
because of dark clouds?

139
00:24:39,280 --> 00:24:43,990
You've gone through such things with
Bala Hatun, gone through such battles...

140
00:24:43,990 --> 00:24:45,820
It can be seen from your scars.

141
00:24:52,480 --> 00:24:56,480
You are brave just like your owner.

142
00:24:57,980 --> 00:25:01,200
You don't give up, you don't surrender.

143
00:25:06,840 --> 00:25:09,360
It's obvious that you do your
horse good, Bala Hatun.

144
00:25:09,360 --> 00:25:12,070
You love him like a friend, ride him
like a foe.

145
00:25:12,970 --> 00:25:16,780
And he endured in silence...

146
00:25:16,780 --> 00:25:20,190
... didn't say anything despite the
infection in his stomach.

147
00:25:23,560 --> 00:25:26,030
For you.

148
00:25:31,890 --> 00:25:34,190
If you have faith in me...

149
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:41,730
... allow me to heal Alaca, like you
saved me from the mud.

150
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:46,600
I have faith in you, so I introduced you
to my father, Osman Bey.

151
00:25:48,870 --> 00:25:50,990
Take care of my horse.

152
00:25:59,340 --> 00:26:03,520
Alaca. Alaca.

153
00:26:14,200 --> 00:26:16,790
It'll take care of the infection in
your stomach.

154
00:26:18,130 --> 00:26:19,870
Now...

155
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:23,490
... I say we take you to the Tent.

156
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:27,320
I'll treat you there. So...

157
00:26:28,490 --> 00:26:34,660
... not another tear falls from your
owner Bala Hatun's beautiful eyes.

158
00:26:48,620 --> 00:26:51,830
May Allah bless you, Osman Bey.

159
00:26:51,980 --> 00:26:54,340
My only wish...

160
00:26:55,320 --> 00:26:59,320
... is you allow me to see you again
in the bazaar tomorrow.

161
00:27:05,060 --> 00:27:10,760
My companion is in your hands.
I allow it, Osman Bey.

162
00:27:12,370 --> 00:27:17,140
No matter what, I'll bring Alaca back.

163
00:27:31,430 --> 00:27:39,550
In the 99 names of Allah, who calls into
being, fills our hearts with faith.

164
00:27:47,640 --> 00:27:55,450
Everyone is awaiting orders to get their
swords, and punish them.

165
00:27:56,550 --> 00:28:00,550
But, Dündar Bey, it seems like
you're stalling us.

166
00:28:04,110 --> 00:28:08,110
I understand your pain and
anger, Bamsı Bey.

167
00:28:09,290 --> 00:28:15,320
But, is it wise to seek battle without
learning the truth?

168
00:28:17,510 --> 00:28:22,940
Dündar Bey, if only wisdom was
needed for battle...

169
00:28:23,150 --> 00:28:26,080
... many small ones couldn't
take over big ones.

170
00:28:29,140 --> 00:28:35,400
What our council lacks is courage,
Dündar Bey.

171
00:28:37,220 --> 00:28:39,550
What it lacks is courage.

172
00:28:43,500 --> 00:28:47,580
My father, Dündar Bey...

173
00:28:49,140 --> 00:28:53,980
... has set his heart to Ertuğrul Bey's
cause.

174
00:28:56,420 --> 00:29:03,440
By doing this, when he was just a
child, he proved his bravery.

175
00:29:05,920 --> 00:29:13,390
Now, no one should try to question
my father's bravery.

176
00:29:24,890 --> 00:29:30,000
We tried trading, they attempted an
assassination.

177
00:29:33,980 --> 00:29:36,210
Our Aybars became a martyr.

178
00:29:37,790 --> 00:29:41,980
My brother Osman is struggling
desperately in a bottomless well.

179
00:29:44,950 --> 00:29:49,200
Battling is our job. But...

180
00:29:50,140 --> 00:29:54,140
... patience, is our guide.

181
00:29:58,130 --> 00:30:03,050
Until we hear from Osman, I say we
don't take action.

182
00:30:22,630 --> 00:30:27,000
- I hope nothing's wrong.
- What is going on?

183
00:30:42,290 --> 00:30:44,160
Thank goodness!

184
00:30:45,600 --> 00:30:49,060
Osman Bey is coming!

185
00:30:51,700 --> 00:30:55,700
Thank goodness! Osman Bey is here.

186
00:31:00,200 --> 00:31:02,650
Thank Allah!

187
00:31:02,650 --> 00:31:05,830
Praise be my Bey! Welcome my Bey!

188
00:31:05,880 --> 00:31:08,040
Take it to the barn.

189
00:31:44,120 --> 00:31:48,120
We can neither leave Osman to infidels...

190
00:31:49,010 --> 00:31:53,010
... nor can we take the chance of battle.

191
00:31:53,360 --> 00:31:55,450
My nephew is right.

192
00:31:56,130 --> 00:32:01,810
It's rather early to go into battle.

193
00:32:02,240 --> 00:32:07,350
We need to wait till Osman returns.

194
00:32:19,140 --> 00:32:21,950
Oh, Osman.

195
00:32:25,690 --> 00:32:31,410
Waiting is useless while treachery is
the matter, Dündar Bey.

196
00:32:32,990 --> 00:32:39,010
I'll tell you if it is war or peace.

197
00:32:44,520 --> 00:32:46,210
Be my guest.

198
00:32:58,670 --> 00:33:02,880
I'm telling you, valiant Beys.

199
00:33:03,890 --> 00:33:08,890
It is time to fight the unrest which has
spread from Kulucahisar.

200
00:33:09,510 --> 00:33:11,490
However...

201
00:33:11,520 --> 00:33:17,480
Fighting with swords only will be nothing
then a cat bite to the enemy.

202
00:33:21,270 --> 00:33:23,470
What do you mean, Osman?

203
00:33:23,800 --> 00:33:28,190
We are facing a tough enemy...

204
00:33:28,700 --> 00:33:32,410
who can strangulate us
with their amplified organs...

205
00:33:33,100 --> 00:33:35,760
as we damage them.

206
00:33:36,750 --> 00:33:42,220
It is time to polish off the infidels
beyond the walls.

207
00:33:45,300 --> 00:33:50,280
The Beys who are here, are
to agree on fighting.

208
00:33:55,340 --> 00:33:57,000
However...

209
00:33:57,780 --> 00:34:01,620
the final decision is Dündar Bey's.

210
00:34:08,990 --> 00:34:13,880
Brother, I didn't realize you grew up
that fast.

211
00:34:13,940 --> 00:34:19,400
In this land, there's no time to be
an immature, brother.

212
00:34:20,910 --> 00:34:26,980
The biggest immaturity is to follow
infidels just to do business.

213
00:34:35,240 --> 00:34:41,420
A decision of war for the Turks' own
benefit should be agreed here today.

214
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:51,420
Otherwise...

215
00:34:52,560 --> 00:34:55,720
You should know that
you'll cut your own throat.

216
00:35:06,410 --> 00:35:13,010
We face the ones who killed their own
governor and set traps for us.

217
00:35:13,540 --> 00:35:19,540
They started this war by killing
my brother Aybars.

218
00:35:20,350 --> 00:35:24,610
We will pray for the battle.

219
00:35:26,180 --> 00:35:31,940
It's the time to be martyrs,
it's not just a war.

220
00:35:38,340 --> 00:35:40,200
That's all I have to say.

221
00:35:41,730 --> 00:35:47,670
Kayı Beys need to rise for war.

222
00:35:48,040 --> 00:35:51,900
It is time to fight!

223
00:35:59,730 --> 00:36:01,630
Osman Bey is right.

224
00:36:01,850 --> 00:36:04,410
The infidels will not behave well.

225
00:36:05,260 --> 00:36:09,070
Eyvallah (Yes) Osman Bey.
It is time to fight.

226
00:36:09,450 --> 00:36:11,820
Now, tell me.

227
00:36:12,980 --> 00:36:17,430
War or peace?

228
00:36:19,140 --> 00:36:22,590
- Beys saying "war" in distance -

229
00:36:22,760 --> 00:36:28,730
If it is a war, then it is a war.
We'd prefer dying to give our Osman, ...

230
00:36:29,830 --> 00:36:32,590
who is entrusted to us by Ertuğrul Bey,
to infidels hands

231
00:36:45,910 --> 00:36:48,240
I see that...

232
00:36:48,770 --> 00:36:51,390
Beys have already decided.

233
00:36:52,190 --> 00:36:55,370
However, this decision...

234
00:36:55,640 --> 00:36:57,970
is beyond me.

235
00:36:58,040 --> 00:37:02,840
We need to be patient till Ertuğrul Bey
returns.

236
00:37:04,980 --> 00:37:07,600
The war decision is Bey's according to
our traditions.

237
00:37:11,570 --> 00:37:13,290
Now...

238
00:37:13,870 --> 00:37:16,020
Excuse me.

239
00:37:16,600 --> 00:37:19,310
I want to talk to my nephews.

240
00:37:20,550 --> 00:37:22,870
Eyvallah (of course)

241
00:38:18,780 --> 00:38:22,230
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(In the name of Allah)

242
00:38:46,380 --> 00:38:49,000
Ya Allah!

243
00:39:23,370 --> 00:39:25,590
Yes, my daughter.

244
00:39:40,300 --> 00:39:42,390
Thanks to you...

245
00:39:42,580 --> 00:39:49,560
This sword, the entrustment of Hz. Ahmet
Yesevi is in our hands, my daughter.

246
00:39:49,880 --> 00:39:53,120
With your prayers, politeness,
in sha Allah, father.

247
00:39:53,140 --> 00:39:57,520
The best politeness is a person's
effort...

248
00:39:57,940 --> 00:40:02,380
and the best prayer is his actions,
my daughter.

249
00:40:03,550 --> 00:40:06,630
You succeded in a very important job.

250
00:40:08,710 --> 00:40:12,000
Because this sword is not like...

251
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:16,960
the other dark sword which sinks
into the heart.

252
00:40:17,300 --> 00:40:20,780
This sword shows up in the most difficult
times and...

253
00:40:21,310 --> 00:40:24,830
reach to the new Hakan ( Turkish ruler )
of the Turks.

254
00:40:25,580 --> 00:40:31,220
When the new Hakan of Turks is equipped
with this...

255
00:40:31,940 --> 00:40:35,760
it'll conquer hearts by demolishing the
infidel lands.

256
00:40:39,690 --> 00:40:42,790
This will give hope to the oppressed, and
fear the cruel...

257
00:40:43,150 --> 00:40:47,420
with the spiritual light which
is spread from here.

258
00:40:50,400 --> 00:40:55,230
How will we find that Hakan among all
those people, father?

259
00:40:55,790 --> 00:40:58,320
Is there a way?

260
00:40:58,420 --> 00:41:00,520
We'll find him, my daughter.

261
00:41:01,340 --> 00:41:07,490
We'll find that spark that didn't blow out
despite the whole winter.

262
00:41:11,700 --> 00:41:16,520
Because, when we connect this sword to
that spark...

263
00:41:16,610 --> 00:41:20,540
it will turn into a volcano...

264
00:41:20,680 --> 00:41:26,550
and it will distribute help to the
oppressed.

265
00:41:26,580 --> 00:41:29,140
Who is that Hakan
( Turkish ruler), father?

266
00:41:29,490 --> 00:41:33,590
He is a man who doesn't hesitate to
fight the cruels.

267
00:41:33,590 --> 00:41:38,200
He is also wise, as well as being strong.

268
00:41:38,200 --> 00:41:42,910
And he helps the oppressed.

269
00:41:44,900 --> 00:41:49,330
He is a man, son of a man.

270
00:42:00,800 --> 00:42:04,720
So, the situation is obvious...

271
00:42:05,120 --> 00:42:08,590
I offer that we shall conquer Kulucahisar
castle.

272
00:42:11,810 --> 00:42:17,060
If we succeeded, we'd conquer
all the castles.

273
00:42:18,310 --> 00:42:24,620
Thus we will be freed of Mongol and
Byzantine attack.

274
00:42:25,420 --> 00:42:29,740
We'll plant Islam's flag everywhere.

275
00:42:31,300 --> 00:42:34,240
Easy, nephew.
Easy.

276
00:42:34,280 --> 00:42:36,410
Why are you so fast?

277
00:42:36,940 --> 00:42:43,790
You stayed in that castle knowing that
you'll be accused of the murder, right?

278
00:42:45,570 --> 00:42:47,720
Yes, uncle.

279
00:42:48,580 --> 00:42:53,350
Because the murderer of the Governor is
also my brother Aybar's murderer.

280
00:42:54,830 --> 00:42:56,510
Osman.

281
00:42:59,230 --> 00:43:02,610
You don't hide anything from us,
do you, brother?

282
00:43:04,600 --> 00:43:08,030
What can I hide after all the information,
brother?

283
00:43:12,960 --> 00:43:19,510
Our efforts on you were worth it, Osman.

284
00:43:20,470 --> 00:43:26,870
You qualified your weapon, and you
qualified being the son of a Bey.

285
00:43:26,870 --> 00:43:30,510
I, as your uncle, am proud of you.

286
00:43:35,320 --> 00:43:39,050
Do you really proud of me despite the
fact that they abducted Aygül, uncle?

287
00:43:40,060 --> 00:43:43,130
The enemy is always evil, nephew.

288
00:43:44,030 --> 00:43:48,430
It's not your fault that what happened to
my daughter.

289
00:43:48,440 --> 00:43:50,450
Eyvallah ( thank you ), uncle.

290
00:43:51,370 --> 00:43:56,960
You dived into the castle like
a blunt dagger.

291
00:43:57,210 --> 00:44:02,550
Infidels held you responsible
for every case.

292
00:44:03,820 --> 00:44:09,060
What I am trying to say is, protect
yourself until Ertuğrul Bey returns.

293
00:44:19,060 --> 00:44:26,220
I trust you, Osman.
Watch out for yourself and your Alps(men).

294
00:44:26,800 --> 00:44:29,470
Don't worry, uncle.

295
00:44:31,690 --> 00:44:34,900
As long as the castle keeps calm...

296
00:44:35,070 --> 00:44:39,790
I can look after myself and my Alps.

297
00:44:53,200 --> 00:44:56,740
May Allah help us.

298
00:45:19,490 --> 00:45:21,700
Excuse me, uncle.

299
00:45:38,010 --> 00:45:43,330
I will find out what you are hiding from
me, and what kind of trouble...

300
00:45:44,090 --> 00:45:46,230
you are in, Osman.

301
00:45:46,800 --> 00:45:50,950
At that time, we'll confront again.

302
00:45:51,960 --> 00:45:53,820
We'll confront.

303
00:46:06,940 --> 00:46:14,240
Master Yannis, the light in your face
tells me that the news is important.

304
00:46:15,050 --> 00:46:18,720
Nizameddin, our man in the bazaar.

305
00:46:19,130 --> 00:46:22,590
He writes about the new bazaar.

306
00:46:22,660 --> 00:46:27,120
- Osman is with them also.
- As I predicted.

307
00:46:28,870 --> 00:46:30,910
Osman is with them.

308
00:46:30,910 --> 00:46:33,950
It is obvious the Ahis (The Ahi Brotherhood)
gathered in new bazaar.

309
00:46:33,950 --> 00:46:38,480
- We need to prevent that.
- We will, Kalanoz, we will.

310
00:46:38,480 --> 00:46:43,120
We will crush the bazaar and kill
all of them.

311
00:46:44,070 --> 00:46:49,110
If I attack them with my soldiers, that
declares the war, but I am ready to fight.

312
00:46:49,110 --> 00:46:51,490
It is too early for a war.

313
00:46:51,800 --> 00:46:56,590
Besides, someone else will do it for you.

314
00:46:56,890 --> 00:47:00,060
Who can do this except for me, Master
Yannis?

315
00:47:38,720 --> 00:47:43,980
Prince Salvador, the bloody blade of
Catalonia.

316
00:47:47,650 --> 00:47:52,080
With my fearless warriors,
I am under your command, Master Yannis.

317
00:48:12,290 --> 00:48:14,040
Alaca.

318
00:48:17,780 --> 00:48:21,160
Come on, here.

319
00:48:21,190 --> 00:48:23,330
Here you go.

320
00:48:29,050 --> 00:48:31,830
My uncle praises me.

321
00:48:33,490 --> 00:48:36,110
He talks so sweetly, Alaca.

322
00:48:37,120 --> 00:48:39,710
It doesn't bode well, does it?

323
00:48:39,900 --> 00:48:42,610
It doesn't bode well.

324
00:48:44,980 --> 00:48:48,610
But, my uncle is a wise man.

325
00:48:50,920 --> 00:48:53,270
He is trying to comfort me...

326
00:48:54,170 --> 00:48:57,240
and then act like who he really is.

327
00:49:05,230 --> 00:49:07,520
Masha Allah. ( touch wood! )

328
00:49:10,580 --> 00:49:13,550
Don't worry, you'll be fine soon.

329
00:49:15,420 --> 00:49:17,510
Come on.

330
00:49:19,530 --> 00:49:22,070
Come on.

331
00:49:26,840 --> 00:49:28,650
Osman Bey.

332
00:49:29,390 --> 00:49:32,310
I was going mad while waiting for
you.

333
00:49:36,200 --> 00:49:38,920
Are you angry with me for what happened?

334
00:49:40,400 --> 00:49:43,220
You have gone through a lot because of me.

335
00:49:43,500 --> 00:49:46,310
I continue living thanks to you.

336
00:49:47,480 --> 00:49:50,020
May Allah be pleased with you.

337
00:49:50,020 --> 00:49:53,350
You are from my blood, Aygül Hatun (lady).

338
00:49:53,630 --> 00:49:56,510
Your life comes first.

339
00:50:06,030 --> 00:50:09,980
Whose horse is this?

340
00:50:09,980 --> 00:50:11,910
Because of the herb he ate.

341
00:50:25,480 --> 00:50:31,460
She is a peddler girl's horse.
I offered my aunt's balm.

342
00:50:31,460 --> 00:50:35,680
I'll take her to the new bazaar and
deliver.

343
00:50:46,020 --> 00:50:49,660
- Be careful, Osman Bey.
- Eyvallah ( Thank you ).

344
00:51:02,150 --> 00:51:03,720
The horse...

345
00:51:04,810 --> 00:51:06,060
eh...

346
00:51:07,290 --> 00:51:11,390
- is a peddler girl's horse.
- a peddler girl?

347
00:51:11,430 --> 00:51:16,540
If a man takes a Hatun's (lady) horse to
her tent...

348
00:51:16,870 --> 00:51:19,800
It means that he loves her.

349
00:51:21,550 --> 00:51:24,480
Alaca, come on.

350
00:51:25,130 --> 00:51:27,100
Come.

351
00:51:28,170 --> 00:51:30,930
Come on, beauty.

352
00:51:53,690 --> 00:51:56,450
Welcome, Gonca Hatun (lady).

353
00:52:11,690 --> 00:52:14,450
Just rest, Bala Hatun.

354
00:52:14,590 --> 00:52:17,210
We've gone through a lot.

355
00:52:17,620 --> 00:52:22,380
You can't imagine how I desperately
want to get back to my job, Gonca Hatun.

356
00:52:28,260 --> 00:52:30,830
Who are they, Bala Hatun (lady)?

357
00:52:45,870 --> 00:52:48,200
A couple of lovers.

358
00:52:49,260 --> 00:52:51,540
Aslı and Kerem.

359
00:52:57,790 --> 00:53:02,910
If they are lovers,
why are they separated?

360
00:53:08,590 --> 00:53:12,230
I heard their story from an Allepon
traveller.

361
00:53:13,730 --> 00:53:18,640
Kerem misses Aslı so much that he
is reduced to his ashes.

362
00:53:21,140 --> 00:53:25,460
And Aslı sweeps the ashes with her
hair.

363
00:53:26,540 --> 00:53:32,530
So, their meeting is due to the judgment
day, and only their story is left for us.

364
00:53:37,880 --> 00:53:42,450
What can I say, Bala? May Allah
give us a love that can be reached.

365
00:53:42,450 --> 00:53:44,170
Amin.

366
00:53:54,340 --> 00:53:58,640
I hope his uncle doesn't get angry when
Osman meets him.

367
00:53:58,740 --> 00:54:03,160
Osman Bey has beaten up the enemy.

368
00:54:03,290 --> 00:54:05,280
Don't worry.

369
00:54:05,890 --> 00:54:08,640
He will get over these, too.

370
00:54:09,330 --> 00:54:10,950
Also...

371
00:54:11,700 --> 00:54:14,110
my Sheik (Bey) has also accepted him.

372
00:54:14,670 --> 00:54:20,710
Would he have accepted him if he hadn't
seen the light in Osman, Gonca Hatun?

373
00:55:01,060 --> 00:55:03,740
Teokles hasn't arrived yet.

374
00:55:03,820 --> 00:55:07,250
Maybe he have been captured by Osman?

375
00:55:09,210 --> 00:55:11,340
Damn it.

376
00:55:11,390 --> 00:55:17,800
If he makes him speak, things will go bad.
It'll be so hard for us to find the treasure.

377
00:55:21,220 --> 00:55:23,790
Commander Andreas!

378
00:55:32,590 --> 00:55:33,970
Yes, madam.

379
00:55:33,970 --> 00:55:38,450
I sent Teoklas after Osman.
He hasn't returned.

380
00:55:38,950 --> 00:55:41,910
Find him, Andreas.

381
00:55:44,060 --> 00:55:49,080
No matter what, find him.

382
00:56:12,470 --> 00:56:15,860
They are hiding what they know from us.

383
00:56:15,860 --> 00:56:20,020
- Can I?
- Come, Samsa.

384
00:56:30,720 --> 00:56:35,560
Long-time no see.
What a surprise to see you, Samsa.

385
00:56:35,560 --> 00:56:39,980
We left you at that castle alone, but...

386
00:56:39,990 --> 00:56:43,370
you were able to manage it.

387
00:56:43,370 --> 00:56:46,030
We are blood brothers, Samsa.

388
00:56:46,030 --> 00:56:49,070
Infidels must have been surprised, too.

389
00:56:49,080 --> 00:56:51,140
Let's sit.

390
00:56:51,490 --> 00:56:57,640
Infidels will panic when Teokles
doesn't show up.

391
00:56:57,640 --> 00:57:01,940
- Who the hell is Teokles?
- The dog they sent to kill me.

392
00:57:01,940 --> 00:57:04,310
Now, we captured him.

393
00:57:04,890 --> 00:57:07,750
I know it, my Osman, I know it.

394
00:57:07,750 --> 00:57:10,710
I know you will take revenge for
my Aybars.

395
00:57:10,710 --> 00:57:14,550
Teokles will lead us to the
murderers of Aybars.

396
00:57:15,670 --> 00:57:20,220
Eyvallah son, Eyvallah ( thank you )

397
00:57:21,930 --> 00:57:27,400
I'll regret them killing a Kayı's valiant.

398
00:57:27,420 --> 00:57:32,360
I, as Erturul Ghazi's son Osman, ...

399
00:57:32,470 --> 00:57:35,860
will skin them to the bones.

400
00:57:35,860 --> 00:57:39,880
- May I?
- Come, Boran Alp.

401
00:57:48,120 --> 00:57:49,990
What happened, Boran?

402
00:57:50,040 --> 00:57:52,410
Why are you looking worried?

403
00:57:53,070 --> 00:57:55,260
Osman Bey...

404
00:57:58,260 --> 00:58:02,310
- Teokles escaped.
- How come?!

405
00:58:04,810 --> 00:58:07,680
I entrusted him to you, didn't I, Boran?

406
00:58:08,820 --> 00:58:10,710
Answer me!

407
00:58:11,140 --> 00:58:14,640
How couldn't you take care of a man whose
ankles and wrists were tied?

408
00:58:14,720 --> 00:58:17,710
Weren't you there?

409
00:58:17,710 --> 00:58:23,110
My Bey, I healed him, then I went to
hunting for him.

410
00:58:23,110 --> 00:58:25,470
He wasn't there when I came back.

411
00:58:25,540 --> 00:58:28,300
The rope was cut by a dagger.

412
00:58:28,300 --> 00:58:32,360
- Someone must have helped.
- Who is that? Who!

413
00:58:32,850 --> 00:58:35,570
Can I, Dündar Bey?

414
00:58:35,660 --> 00:58:38,600
Come, son, come.

415
00:58:47,690 --> 00:58:51,940
- I have something to tell you, father.
- Go on.

416
00:58:54,070 --> 00:58:56,150
Osman.

417
00:58:56,250 --> 00:58:58,640
What did he do?

418
00:58:58,820 --> 00:59:03,470
He captured one of Sofia's hunters,
Teokles.

419
00:59:06,270 --> 00:59:08,000
Where is he?

420
00:59:08,120 --> 00:59:11,460
Don't worry, father. I saved him
from Osman's hands

421
00:59:11,460 --> 00:59:14,990
Could you receive any information?

422
00:59:15,250 --> 00:59:18,850
After Osman escaped
from the castle, she sent him to get him.

423
00:59:18,850 --> 00:59:19,910
Who sent him?

424
00:59:19,960 --> 00:59:21,620
Sofia.

425
00:59:21,870 --> 00:59:23,280
Sofia.

426
00:59:34,100 --> 00:59:39,750
Osman beat up Teokles so bad, but he
is fine now.

427
00:59:39,900 --> 00:59:43,710
Where is that infidel now?

428
00:59:43,710 --> 00:59:45,870
We have him, father.

429
00:59:48,800 --> 00:59:53,590
This information will save Bithynia from a
huge war.

430
00:59:53,610 --> 00:59:57,970
Inform Gündüz Bey.
Off you go.

431
01:00:17,670 --> 01:00:22,400
Jackals go to their nooks,
bears go to their caves.

432
01:00:24,810 --> 01:00:27,700
The place where he is going to is obvious.

433
01:00:27,760 --> 01:00:29,560
The castle.

434
01:00:32,010 --> 01:00:36,690
I'll shoot the jackal in its corner,
I'll choke the bear in the cave!

435
01:00:38,100 --> 01:00:41,760
My Osman, those infidels are playful.

436
01:00:41,840 --> 01:00:45,690
This may be a trap to draw you into
the castle.

437
01:00:46,920 --> 01:00:51,220
We need to turn that castle into a grave
for Teokles, so that...

438
01:00:51,380 --> 01:00:56,000
no one can dare to escape from Osman
Bey from now on.

439
01:00:56,660 --> 01:01:01,020
And when we kill him, it'll be a lesson
to everyone.

440
01:01:02,280 --> 01:01:07,130
Sergeant Samsa, it is time to hunt
the castle.

441
01:01:08,680 --> 01:01:12,140
Those animals know me very well.

442
01:01:12,380 --> 01:01:15,040
They haven't face me recently.

443
01:01:16,040 --> 01:01:20,360
The castle will be a good choice,
in sha'Allah. Long live, my valiant!

444
01:01:20,360 --> 01:01:23,500
You made me happy.

445
01:01:31,870 --> 01:01:35,730
- Speaking in Greek -

446
01:02:16,160 --> 01:02:22,150
In God's holy spirit, the bond
in your eyes disappeared now, Kalanoz.

447
01:02:38,060 --> 01:02:45,180
Do you swear on fighting the Turks in the
way of Holy Margarit Church?

448
01:02:48,000 --> 01:02:49,960
I do.

449
01:02:50,950 --> 01:02:55,290
Do you swear on fighting
everything that...

450
01:02:55,290 --> 01:02:59,290
Turk's consider as holy?

451
01:03:00,550 --> 01:03:02,630
I do.

452
01:03:04,910 --> 01:03:07,790
God bless you.

453
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:25,980
I was ready to raid the new bazaar with my
soldiers, Master Yannis.

454
01:03:26,030 --> 01:03:28,490
I hope Catalans can manage it.

455
01:03:28,490 --> 01:03:34,890
I don't have any doubts, Kalanoz.
You'll do much more when the time comes.

456
01:03:34,890 --> 01:03:39,070
But as you said, they shouldn't suspect
the castle.

457
01:03:39,070 --> 01:03:42,060
Freeze their tent.

458
01:03:42,060 --> 01:03:48,060
The days that we'll kill all of them...

459
01:03:49,150 --> 01:03:51,120
are close, Kalanoz.

460
01:03:51,120 --> 01:03:57,950
But now, we are going to take care of all
the Ahis, and we will not be involved in.

461
01:03:57,950 --> 01:04:01,760
What's more, we'll take back the holy
entrustment.

462
01:04:01,960 --> 01:04:06,740
If the owner of the wood sword
owns it via Edebali, ...

463
01:04:06,970 --> 01:04:09,430
we'll wake the sleeping up.

464
01:04:09,830 --> 01:04:12,540
-Do you understand me?
-Yes, sir.

465
01:04:21,090 --> 01:04:23,340
Welcome aboard, son.

466
01:04:43,560 --> 01:04:46,270
What you told me warmed my heart, Edebali.

467
01:04:46,690 --> 01:04:49,720
This should be such a state that...

468
01:04:50,840 --> 01:04:54,050
justice should revive with it.

469
01:04:54,210 --> 01:04:56,840
The Islam community should find peace.

470
01:04:57,170 --> 01:04:59,720
The cruel should be afraid.

471
01:05:01,000 --> 01:05:05,000
Our morality should uprise.

472
01:05:15,290 --> 01:05:19,290
A`udhu billahi min ash-shaytan ar-rajim...
( I seek protection in Allah from the accursed shaytan)

473
01:05:20,640 --> 01:05:23,800
Bismillahir rahmanir rahim.
(In the name of Allah, the Most Beneficent, the Most Merciful)

474
01:05:25,370 --> 01:05:28,180
"Indeed, We have given you, [ O Muhammad ],"

475
01:05:28,200 --> 01:05:30,640
"a clear conquest"

476
01:05:31,020 --> 01:05:35,020
"That, Allah...

477
01:05:35,200 --> 01:05:39,150
....may forgive for you what preceded of your sin and what will follow"

478
01:05:39,220 --> 01:05:43,220
"And complete his favor upon you and guide you to a straight path"

479
01:05:43,220 --> 01:05:46,120
"will make sure that
you're on the right way."

480
01:05:46,760 --> 01:05:50,740
"And that Allah
may help thee with powerful help"

481
01:05:50,780 --> 01:05:56,480
"It is he Who sent down tranquilitty into the hearts of the believers,

482
01:05:57,020 --> 01:06:02,250
That they may add faith to their faith"

483
01:06:03,420 --> 01:06:07,420
"Allah belong the armies of
the heavens and the earth"

484
01:06:07,910 --> 01:06:11,640
"And Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise"

485
01:06:12,390 --> 01:06:16,680
"That He may admit
the men and women...

486
01:06:16,680 --> 01:06:20,680
Who believe, to gardens
beneath which rivers flow,

487
01:06:20,720 --> 01:06:22,730
"To abide therein eternally.."

488
01:06:23,290 --> 01:06:34,840
"And remove from them their misdeeds and ever is that, in the sight of Allah, the highest achievement."

489
01:06:38,160 --> 01:06:40,340
"Sadaqa Allaah al-'Azeem."
(Allah Almighty has spoken the truth.)

490
01:06:45,330 --> 01:06:47,450
My Allah...

491
01:06:48,500 --> 01:06:50,490
You're the one who sees...

492
01:06:51,150 --> 01:06:52,820
knows...

493
01:06:53,480 --> 01:06:55,750
and creates everything.

494
01:06:56,770 --> 01:06:58,840
I don't hide anything from you.

495
01:07:00,570 --> 01:07:04,130
Even the most unknown comes
out if it comes to you.

496
01:07:05,520 --> 01:07:08,090
You're the one who knows about
my biggest dreams...

497
01:07:09,830 --> 01:07:12,360
that are beyond me...

498
01:07:12,790 --> 01:07:15,730
my mad passions...

499
01:07:16,000 --> 01:07:20,000
and my thoughts and dreams
that are beyond this land.

500
01:07:22,550 --> 01:07:25,770
You, who have given
me these dreams, this love...

501
01:07:26,440 --> 01:07:28,870
and this passion,

502
01:07:30,920 --> 01:07:34,620
will give me the power.

503
01:07:39,280 --> 01:07:40,930
Oh My Allah.

504
01:07:42,640 --> 01:07:44,470
I had a dream.

505
01:07:47,060 --> 01:07:49,110
Make it real.

506
01:07:50,300 --> 01:07:54,300
Let me carry my father's flag further.

507
01:07:55,320 --> 01:07:58,240
I was in the land when I opened my eyes.

508
01:08:00,370 --> 01:08:04,020
Let me see beyond the waters.

509
01:08:06,440 --> 01:08:10,410
Everywhere is hazy and thick.

510
01:08:11,010 --> 01:08:13,830
We are surrounded by enemies.

511
01:08:14,560 --> 01:08:17,640
With İlay-ı Kelimetullah
(exalting Islam)...

512
01:08:19,330 --> 01:08:23,750
let me enlighten the dark, my Allah.

513
01:08:26,410 --> 01:08:27,960
Amin.

514
01:08:42,580 --> 01:08:43,520
Uncle...

515
01:08:44,810 --> 01:08:47,370
You're right but...

516
01:08:48,790 --> 01:08:52,790
The sky is hazy, the water is blurry.

517
01:08:54,590 --> 01:08:57,930
After all these problems, how will
we trust these infidels?

518
01:08:58,930 --> 01:09:01,510
What if they do something bad?

519
01:09:03,440 --> 01:09:06,240
Fox is the most crafty but...

520
01:09:06,620 --> 01:09:10,620
the bazaar is full of its
fleece, Gündüz Bey.

521
01:09:18,420 --> 01:09:20,530
I care about Osman.

522
01:09:20,670 --> 01:09:24,670
When he hears that we've given Teokles
to the castle, he'll be very angry.

523
01:09:24,910 --> 01:09:27,240
We don't know what he'll do.

524
01:09:29,400 --> 01:09:30,790
Gündüz Bey.

525
01:09:30,950 --> 01:09:32,480
What should we do?

526
01:09:33,310 --> 01:09:37,310
Just for Osman will be angry, will
we fight Kulucahisar?

527
01:09:42,630 --> 01:09:43,820
Uncle.

528
01:09:44,570 --> 01:09:46,860
My father Ertuğrul Bey will return soon.

529
01:09:47,900 --> 01:09:50,170
He'll want to know who's behind the...

530
01:09:50,230 --> 01:09:53,970
murder of Aybars and Governor.

531
01:09:55,310 --> 01:09:59,550
Osman was seen in the castle
that night, so I say that...

532
01:09:59,550 --> 01:10:02,110
we shouldn't give our only proof to them.

533
01:10:05,840 --> 01:10:07,930
We shouldn't but...

534
01:10:08,660 --> 01:10:10,420
what will we do?

535
01:10:12,880 --> 01:10:16,880
Do you think that only they have
the traitors inside their castle?

536
01:10:25,170 --> 01:10:28,420
If they know that we have Teokles...

537
01:10:29,440 --> 01:10:33,440
isn't it a cause of war for them that
Osman was seen in the castle?

538
01:10:37,780 --> 01:10:42,690
Till my brother returns, the trade
agreement with Kulucahisar will continue.

539
01:10:44,290 --> 01:10:46,210
I can't ruin the...

540
01:10:46,210 --> 01:10:50,130
peace he has created because of Osman.

541
01:10:53,650 --> 01:10:55,350
But...

542
01:10:55,450 --> 01:10:58,000
Osman shouldn't know about it.

543
01:11:01,090 --> 01:11:02,390
Now...

544
01:11:02,510 --> 01:11:04,550
where's that bastard?

545
01:11:05,230 --> 01:11:08,260
I tied him in a nook behind Karanlıkdere.

546
01:11:08,410 --> 01:11:10,360
Even the devil can't find him.

547
01:11:10,400 --> 01:11:12,380
Let's go then.

548
01:11:54,670 --> 01:11:55,800
Son...

549
01:11:58,700 --> 01:12:00,260
Moon son... (Ay)

550
01:12:01,830 --> 01:12:03,660
Aybars son...

551
01:12:05,270 --> 01:12:06,830
Brave son...

552
01:12:07,190 --> 01:12:09,520
When I saw you hungry...

553
01:12:10,910 --> 01:12:14,140
I fed you.

554
01:12:14,910 --> 01:12:18,260
When I saw you undressed, I dressed you.

555
01:12:20,150 --> 01:12:24,150
I had gone long way.

556
01:12:25,950 --> 01:12:29,950
I shed blood, I sacrificed
an animal for you.

557
01:12:30,960 --> 01:12:34,960
With a wish and a pray...

558
01:12:36,790 --> 01:12:39,550
I found a son.

559
01:12:43,210 --> 01:12:45,050
I found you.

560
01:12:45,770 --> 01:12:47,710
I found you.

561
01:12:51,730 --> 01:12:54,100
I found you, son.

562
01:13:17,960 --> 01:13:21,060
Esselamu Aleykum ve Rahmetullah...
("May the peace and mercy of Allah be with you")

563
01:13:22,030 --> 01:13:25,050
Esselamu Aleykum ve Rahmetullah.
("May the peace and mercy of Allah be with you")

564
01:13:57,870 --> 01:14:00,160
The infidels are not that fast.

565
01:14:00,330 --> 01:14:02,280
I recognized you, Tursun.

566
01:14:07,310 --> 01:14:09,590
Who are you?

567
01:14:11,220 --> 01:14:13,240
Osman Bey sent me.

568
01:14:13,700 --> 01:14:15,520
What's it?

569
01:14:17,100 --> 01:14:19,410
Why did you come to the castle?

570
01:14:19,830 --> 01:14:22,300
I'm looking for someone named Teokles.

571
01:14:29,680 --> 01:14:31,780
Tell me from the beginning.

572
01:15:13,350 --> 01:15:15,690
Osman Bey talked.

573
01:15:15,760 --> 01:15:18,340
He'll come the castle in the end.

574
01:15:19,150 --> 01:15:20,680
But...

575
01:15:20,760 --> 01:15:24,470
I don't know if he has come ever.

576
01:15:26,880 --> 01:15:28,380
Wait...

577
01:15:28,520 --> 01:15:32,460
Don't worry about it. We'll find him...

578
01:15:32,580 --> 01:15:34,540
no matter what.

579
01:15:44,540 --> 01:15:46,240
What are these sounds?

580
01:16:05,540 --> 01:16:08,630
Dündar Bey and Gündüz Bey.

581
01:16:14,230 --> 01:16:16,610
And Teokles.

582
01:16:20,700 --> 01:16:24,040
Now it's clear who got him.

583
01:17:24,020 --> 01:17:25,400
The Great Father.

584
01:17:26,650 --> 01:17:28,620
The Great Father.

585
01:17:30,230 --> 01:17:31,650
It's good to see you.

586
01:17:33,180 --> 01:17:36,550
-We're very happy.
-You're welcome!

587
01:17:37,370 --> 01:17:42,630
It's so good to see you, comrade
Nizamettin.

588
01:17:43,030 --> 01:17:48,810
In a short time, we wish to have
conversations with friends.

589
01:17:49,010 --> 01:17:51,160
We're friendly all.

590
01:17:52,150 --> 01:17:54,880
Many friends know about it.

591
01:17:55,370 --> 01:17:57,680
You should know it too.

592
01:17:57,900 --> 01:18:00,820
With pleasure.

593
01:18:08,040 --> 01:18:09,550
Where are they?

594
01:18:10,170 --> 01:18:13,350
There, near the potter stall.

595
01:18:49,570 --> 01:18:53,490
I was assassinated in your
castle, I remained silent.

596
01:18:54,870 --> 01:18:57,800
You charged my nephew with murder,

597
01:18:58,490 --> 01:19:00,080
I stood for it.

598
01:19:05,410 --> 01:19:08,800
Burçin, the bride of Bamsı Bey
who is one of the Beys of our tent...

599
01:19:09,380 --> 01:19:12,940
was pounded up by you. I was silent.

600
01:19:13,300 --> 01:19:15,110
You abducted my daughter...

601
01:19:15,300 --> 01:19:17,590
My Aygül...

602
01:19:18,040 --> 01:19:20,330
I passed over it.

603
01:19:21,730 --> 01:19:25,900
You put this murderer on my
nephew Osman's tail...

604
01:19:26,880 --> 01:19:29,840
I brought to you with my own hands.

605
01:19:31,230 --> 01:19:32,540
Dündar Bey...

606
01:19:33,400 --> 01:19:36,940
We're so unhappy for what happened. ..

607
01:19:41,280 --> 01:19:43,200
but don't forget that...

608
01:19:46,520 --> 01:19:48,860
my husband was murdered.

609
01:19:50,730 --> 01:19:54,730
Your husband was my friend.

610
01:19:54,820 --> 01:19:58,890
The murder of your friend's suspect
is your nephew Osman.

611
01:19:59,890 --> 01:20:04,080
He escaped from our castle,
not to be on trial.

612
01:20:04,500 --> 01:20:07,050
You sent murderers after him...

613
01:20:07,550 --> 01:20:10,070
to kill him.

614
01:20:10,740 --> 01:20:12,080
Dündar Bey...

615
01:20:12,750 --> 01:20:17,390
if Osman is put on trial and prove
that he's not guilty...

616
01:20:17,460 --> 01:20:19,800
there'll be no problem.

617
01:20:19,820 --> 01:20:22,700
I wish you'd obey our justice to...

618
01:20:22,750 --> 01:20:25,110
show your goodwill and...

619
01:20:25,570 --> 01:20:28,830
brought Osman instead of him.

620
01:20:30,010 --> 01:20:32,580
I last saw Osman in this castle.

621
01:20:33,280 --> 01:20:36,310
If he runs away from a castle
that you secure...

622
01:20:37,070 --> 01:20:39,320
I have nothing to do.

623
01:20:43,270 --> 01:20:44,850
Osman...

624
01:20:45,950 --> 01:20:47,620
will be on trial.

625
01:20:48,510 --> 01:20:50,330
But not here.

626
01:20:50,530 --> 01:20:54,530
In a Söğüt court...

627
01:20:54,820 --> 01:20:56,790
where there are Greeks and Kayıs.

628
01:21:14,250 --> 01:21:17,320
I'm a truth-seeking, Dündar Bey.

629
01:21:24,290 --> 01:21:27,070
I accept your proposal.

630
01:21:30,770 --> 01:21:33,120
Then, here you are.

631
01:22:18,870 --> 01:22:21,120
Go to your room, Teokles.

632
01:22:25,300 --> 01:22:27,150
Have some rest.

633
01:22:38,090 --> 01:22:39,210
The door!

634
01:23:10,330 --> 01:23:12,630
-Feed the horses.
-Okay, my Bey.

635
01:23:13,110 --> 01:23:15,910
-You stay here.
-Okay, my Bey.

636
01:23:24,270 --> 01:23:28,850
Thief! Thief! Help me!

637
01:23:28,990 --> 01:23:29,890
Help me!

638
01:23:43,830 --> 01:23:46,370
Run! My golds!

639
01:25:13,160 --> 01:25:14,500
My Bey...

640
01:25:15,050 --> 01:25:17,170
My Bey... please forgive me.

641
01:25:21,820 --> 01:25:23,930
Please spare my life, my Bey.

642
01:25:29,630 --> 01:25:31,150
Please, my Bey.

643
01:25:39,140 --> 01:25:40,910
Nizamettin Bey!

644
01:25:43,970 --> 01:25:46,410
I'll punish them.

645
01:25:50,720 --> 01:25:52,640
If I see them here again...

646
01:25:53,690 --> 01:25:56,050
they will die.

647
01:26:02,770 --> 01:26:06,950
They deserved it. Long live, Osman Bey.

648
01:26:07,240 --> 01:26:10,760
Do your duty properly, Nizamettin Bey.

649
01:26:16,020 --> 01:26:20,010
Remember your vow that
there'll be no injustice.

650
01:26:24,190 --> 01:26:26,280
If this happens again...

651
01:26:26,730 --> 01:26:28,570
I'll call you to account.

652
01:26:49,750 --> 01:26:51,990
If someone's insolent, his
tongue will be cut.

653
01:26:51,990 --> 01:26:54,060
If someone's a thief, his
hand will be cut.

654
01:26:55,760 --> 01:26:58,270
He deserved it, Osman Bey.

655
01:27:02,240 --> 01:27:04,070
Take these thieves.

656
01:27:22,680 --> 01:27:24,600
Are you looking for your pouch?

657
01:27:25,470 --> 01:27:28,300
Thank you so much. God bless you.

658
01:27:31,470 --> 01:27:33,550
Are you Osman Bey?

659
01:27:34,060 --> 01:27:35,910
Ertuğrul Bey's son.

660
01:27:36,840 --> 01:27:38,810
You're brave like your father.

661
01:27:40,300 --> 01:27:42,410
God grant you to your loved ones....

662
01:27:42,430 --> 01:27:45,880
and grant us to your fair hands.

663
01:27:46,520 --> 01:27:47,890
Thank you so much.

664
01:27:54,100 --> 01:27:55,710
God bless you.

665
01:27:56,040 --> 01:27:57,640
Thank you.

666
01:28:13,860 --> 01:28:16,090
Aslı and Kerem.

667
01:28:19,040 --> 01:28:22,000
I worked hard for it. It's done.

668
01:28:23,860 --> 01:28:26,180
Great job. It looks beautiful.

669
01:28:29,060 --> 01:28:33,060
But the only thing that is
done is not the tile.

670
01:28:48,380 --> 01:28:50,560
You're very brave, son.

671
01:28:51,930 --> 01:28:55,100
May your fair sword be everlasting.

672
01:28:56,410 --> 01:28:58,840
Thanks, Great Father.

673
01:28:58,960 --> 01:29:00,920
Where do you come from?
Where are you going?

674
01:29:01,010 --> 01:29:05,010
We come from Hayy (Allah),
we go to Hu. (Allah)

675
01:29:05,390 --> 01:29:08,010
We go to Allah with our hearts...

676
01:29:08,290 --> 01:29:11,070
and we travel with our feet.

677
01:29:13,750 --> 01:29:17,540
-May your travel be holy, Great Father.
-Thanks.

678
01:29:33,020 --> 01:29:37,320
I've been travelling all my life but I've
never seen anything like this.

679
01:29:42,090 --> 01:29:45,130
It's priceless but...

680
01:29:46,400 --> 01:29:48,260
how much does it cost, daughter?

681
01:29:48,340 --> 01:29:49,790
You're welcome.

682
01:29:50,190 --> 01:29:53,610
Money comes from people but
Allah gives the abundance.

683
01:29:54,650 --> 01:29:58,650
-It's my gift for you, Great Father.
-Thanks, daughter.

684
01:29:58,830 --> 01:30:01,360
I hope you'll always be happy.

685
01:30:08,310 --> 01:30:12,310
When a lover meets lover,
they become happy.

686
01:30:14,540 --> 01:30:16,100
They become happy.

687
01:30:23,450 --> 01:30:27,830
May Allah watch over you two, farewell.

688
01:30:46,820 --> 01:30:51,580
- What is it, Osman Bey?
- Many wolves wear sheep hides.

689
01:30:51,840 --> 01:30:56,530
And many traitors look like dervishes
wearing circlets and sweaters.

690
01:31:01,910 --> 01:31:04,690
I didn't like this man at all.
You should know.

691
01:31:06,780 --> 01:31:11,120
Neither traitors give up betraying,
nor tyrants give up their tyranny.

692
01:31:12,110 --> 01:31:15,530
We should just stay in the right way.

693
01:31:19,950 --> 01:31:24,440
- Gonca Hatun, you take care of the stall.
- Don't worry.

694
01:31:45,530 --> 01:31:49,530
So he is the Osman Bey,
son of Ertuğrul Gazi.

695
01:31:49,590 --> 01:31:53,390
- He is going to be trouble in the raid.
- Kill Osman in the raid.

696
01:31:53,450 --> 01:31:57,450
But I want Bala,
Edebali's daughter alive.

697
01:31:58,420 --> 01:32:02,820
- We will get what we want from her.
- How did you find out it was Bala Hatun?

698
01:32:03,260 --> 01:32:07,590
I saw her when I came to their
door to be a follower of Ahî Evran.

699
01:32:09,000 --> 01:32:12,240
She was with her father,
she was little back then.

700
01:32:13,290 --> 01:32:17,290
But her eyes, they look the same.

701
01:32:30,200 --> 01:32:35,200
- It came here like the wind.
- How did you cure my Alaca, Osman Bey?

702
01:32:35,900 --> 01:32:39,900
- What was its remedy?
- Its remedy is a little bit balm.

703
01:32:40,940 --> 01:32:43,970
And its love for you, Bala Hatun.

704
01:32:45,640 --> 01:32:49,640
It was so impatient to go to
many adventures with you.

705
01:32:49,730 --> 01:32:54,190
You see, Osman Bey? I am just a
poor artisan on the way of Ahî.

706
01:33:10,780 --> 01:33:13,720
When I saw you weeping near the horse...

707
01:33:15,790 --> 01:33:19,940
- ... I made a promise to myself.
- What promise was that?

708
01:33:20,930 --> 01:33:24,930
I said whoever upsets this Hatun(Lady)...

709
01:33:27,050 --> 01:33:29,980
... is my sworn enemy.

710
01:33:43,830 --> 01:33:48,620
Only the ones we love can upset us,
not our enemies, Osman Bey.

711
01:33:50,020 --> 01:33:52,430
Don't you worry about it.

712
01:34:05,400 --> 01:34:07,280
Osman Bey!

713
01:34:15,430 --> 01:34:17,220
What do you want, bully?

714
01:34:17,730 --> 01:34:20,970
Alişar Bey sent word everywhere,
my Bey. He is looking for you.

715
01:34:21,190 --> 01:34:24,710
He said he wants to welcome you
in his mansion, not as a banner lord...

716
01:34:24,710 --> 01:34:26,420
... but as a hunting friend.

717
01:34:28,550 --> 01:34:31,740
Thank you, we can go there together.

718
01:34:38,480 --> 01:34:43,100
Farewell, Bala Hatun. I will come
to see you as soon as possible.

719
01:35:26,460 --> 01:35:28,800
Osman Bey sends his regards.

720
01:35:29,490 --> 01:35:30,370
Stop!

721
01:35:42,060 --> 01:35:46,190
As Byzantine is full of bastards,
Kayı is full of brave men.

722
01:36:31,010 --> 01:36:32,500
Osman Bey.

723
01:36:41,680 --> 01:36:42,990
Welcome.

724
01:36:43,430 --> 01:36:47,180
- Thank you, Alişar Bey.
- Come in.

725
01:36:53,420 --> 01:36:56,990
Let me serve you basil sherbet, Osman Bey.

726
01:37:00,530 --> 01:37:04,320
I've heard you ruined Kulucahisar Castle.

727
01:37:04,470 --> 01:37:07,300
We are breathing down their necks.

728
01:37:08,610 --> 01:37:11,500
They will see us even in their shadows.

729
01:37:11,980 --> 01:37:17,020
We will surely won't let their slanders,
treacheries go without punishment.

730
01:37:24,860 --> 01:37:27,670
I know you didn't kill the governor.

731
01:37:28,600 --> 01:37:33,300
Because if you had killed him,
not a soul could've known about it.

732
01:37:33,380 --> 01:37:37,380
You would've got out of
that damned castle easily.

733
01:37:41,960 --> 01:37:45,610
If I had doubted you for a second...

734
01:37:47,270 --> 01:37:51,470
As a banner lord, I would've
found you before your uncle...

735
01:37:52,030 --> 01:37:56,670
... thrown you to a dungeon,
had you stand on trial before kadi.

736
01:37:57,810 --> 01:38:01,050
I will drown them with
their own treachery, Alişar Bey.

737
01:38:01,560 --> 01:38:06,510
I will find both of the governor's and
my brother's killers and punish them.

738
01:38:08,430 --> 01:38:11,520
I also want a trial for this.

739
01:38:12,610 --> 01:38:17,570
I want to come to the trial
by myself and be judged.

740
01:38:46,360 --> 01:38:48,470
When we...

741
01:38:49,150 --> 01:38:51,450
... first left this table...

742
01:38:51,820 --> 01:38:54,720
... we were very hopeful.

743
01:38:55,180 --> 01:38:57,580
I assure you Princess Sofia.

744
01:38:57,940 --> 01:39:04,580
My friend Yorgopolos' death,
hurt us the most after you.

745
01:39:05,250 --> 01:39:08,880
When my husband's killer is punished...

746
01:39:09,110 --> 01:39:13,110
... we will renew that
friendship, Dündar Bey.

747
01:39:13,230 --> 01:39:19,340
A permanent peace in these lands
was our biggest dream with Yorgopolos.

748
01:39:20,600 --> 01:39:25,870
Moreover, the most important
legacy that he left is this.

749
01:39:36,780 --> 01:39:38,160
Ma'am.

750
01:39:39,320 --> 01:39:42,030
Theokoles has been killed.

751
01:39:46,770 --> 01:39:48,290
How?

752
01:39:55,200 --> 01:39:56,640
Osman!

753
01:39:58,520 --> 01:40:00,010
He did this!

754
01:40:00,220 --> 01:40:03,690
Osman isn't even here,
Princess, how could that happen?

755
01:40:03,790 --> 01:40:05,990
Only Osman could have done this!

756
01:40:06,310 --> 01:40:07,800
Enough!

757
01:40:14,200 --> 01:40:18,200
The traitors killed your governor too.

758
01:40:18,760 --> 01:40:22,550
We were starting to believe you.

759
01:40:22,810 --> 01:40:26,460
We will discuss this in
the trial, Dündar Bey.

760
01:40:27,880 --> 01:40:33,520
If my nephew is found innocent in the trial
and you still continue to fight him...

761
01:40:34,460 --> 01:40:37,350
... then have it your way.

762
01:40:40,270 --> 01:40:45,700
War, or peace, so be it.

763
01:40:49,020 --> 01:40:52,510
You better know it like this.

764
01:41:26,110 --> 01:41:31,790
So you think the killer of Bamsı Bey's
son and the governor is the same person.

765
01:41:33,730 --> 01:41:38,860
You sneaked into the castle to talk
with the governor for this reason, right?

766
01:41:39,640 --> 01:41:43,830
Right, I also spoke with
governor before he died.

767
01:41:45,390 --> 01:41:49,960
You did? Then tell me everything you know.

768
01:41:50,660 --> 01:41:55,820
The governor told me that the treachery
was spreading from his castle, Alişar Bey.

769
01:41:56,750 --> 01:42:01,800
I was the only one he trusted, neither
his wife nor his Commander Kolonoz.

770
01:42:07,780 --> 01:42:12,870
The war is close, Osman Bey,
and this is no time to be silent.

771
01:42:13,600 --> 01:42:18,600
The war between Kayı and Kulucahisar...

772
01:42:19,690 --> 01:42:23,690
... became a war between
the Seljuk and Byzantine.

773
01:42:24,840 --> 01:42:30,460
Princess Sofia and Commander Kolonoz
wanted you to be put on a trial.

774
01:42:31,260 --> 01:42:34,640
You escaped from the dungeon too.

775
01:42:35,260 --> 01:42:38,340
The trial should be on our lands.

776
01:42:38,650 --> 01:42:43,330
- Why? What are you afraid of?
- Princess Sofia...

777
01:42:43,900 --> 01:42:46,140
... Commander Kolonoz...

778
01:42:46,740 --> 01:42:49,920
... they wanted to kill me
before I was on trial.

779
01:42:54,220 --> 01:42:59,380
- You must have strong evidence for that.
- You can be sure about that, Alişar Bey.

780
01:43:00,200 --> 01:43:06,040
When the trial begins, everyone will see.
I will prove both of them are the killers.

781
01:43:06,380 --> 01:43:10,210
What are you talking about Osman Bey,
do you have any idea what...

782
01:43:10,400 --> 01:43:13,710
-... will that lead to?
- As long as you stand with the truth...

783
01:43:14,350 --> 01:43:17,830
... they should be afraid, not me.

784
01:43:29,610 --> 01:43:35,070
I say, if they are the target of a
hunter like you, they are doomed.

785
01:43:35,340 --> 01:43:39,340
If we draw them to our hunting grounds...

786
01:43:39,560 --> 01:43:42,150
... I will make them sing
like nightingales.

787
01:43:42,550 --> 01:43:46,840
You just need to trust me, Alişar Bey.

788
01:43:48,790 --> 01:43:53,210
You have my word, Osman
Bey, I will do what it takes.

789
01:44:39,830 --> 01:44:43,830
Did you see that man?
I crushed his head with my axe!

790
01:44:53,310 --> 01:44:55,990
We smashed them up!

791
01:45:29,540 --> 01:45:32,450
Brave sons of Catalonia!

792
01:45:32,790 --> 01:45:35,960
Lion-hearted warriors of Prince Salvador!

793
01:45:36,780 --> 01:45:41,160
Are you ready to leave
terrible nightmares after you?

794
01:45:43,350 --> 01:45:45,730
- Are you ready?
- Yes!

795
01:45:45,930 --> 01:45:48,280
- Are you ready?
- Yes!

796
01:45:50,850 --> 01:45:55,060
They will call us "ruthless
warriors of Prince Salvador"!

797
01:45:56,300 --> 01:45:59,160
They will scare their
children with our stories.

798
01:46:00,410 --> 01:46:03,830
Pregnant women will miscarry
when they hear our names!

799
01:46:06,840 --> 01:46:10,840
Young boys' hairs will
turn grey from the fear!

800
01:46:14,750 --> 01:46:19,950
For Prince Salvador! For the
treasures waiting for us!

801
01:46:20,160 --> 01:46:24,160
- Now is the time for battle!
- Salvador!

802
01:46:24,270 --> 01:46:32,110
Salvador!

803
01:46:43,860 --> 01:46:46,010
Are you sure, Sergeant Samsa?

804
01:46:46,260 --> 01:46:48,330
Like my faith, Osman Bey.

805
01:46:58,820 --> 01:47:02,820
My uncle, my brother!

806
01:47:03,590 --> 01:47:05,180
Batur!

807
01:47:08,750 --> 01:47:11,690
I saw it myself.

808
01:47:12,120 --> 01:47:16,190
That infidel called Theokoles was
between Dündar Bey and Gündüz Bey.

809
01:47:16,420 --> 01:47:17,910
Batur was behind them.

810
01:47:18,030 --> 01:47:20,990
So they handed the man who
Princess Sofia hired to kill me...

811
01:47:21,140 --> 01:47:25,710
... the biggest leverage I had to find my
brother Aybars' killers to the castle?

812
01:47:28,000 --> 01:47:30,580
Both my uncle and my
brother was in the tent.

813
01:47:32,780 --> 01:47:33,630
So...

814
01:47:35,220 --> 01:47:39,760
... Batur is the one who went
after Bora and kidnapped Theokoles.

815
01:47:41,530 --> 01:47:43,170
Batur, huh?

816
01:47:44,140 --> 01:47:45,340
Batur, huh?

817
01:47:45,590 --> 01:47:47,570
Batur, Batur!

818
01:47:48,370 --> 01:47:51,130
He will pay for this treachery!

819
01:47:51,320 --> 01:47:53,150
What are you going to do, Osman Bey?

820
01:47:55,120 --> 01:48:00,730
I will put them on the most righteous
trial, Konur Alp! I will make the trial!

821
01:48:01,450 --> 01:48:07,040
My witnesses will be my martyr brother
Aybars, and Yorgopolos who was killed.

822
01:48:07,590 --> 01:48:12,610
The kadi of my trial will be my anger,
the executioner will be my sword!

823
01:48:15,200 --> 01:48:17,540
I will judge them myself!

824
01:48:23,080 --> 01:48:27,720
They didn't say "There's good in
every bad." for nothing, Gündüz.

825
01:48:28,060 --> 01:48:35,720
You are right uncle, Theokoles' death
also proved my brother Osman's innocence.

826
01:48:44,610 --> 01:48:48,030
You are just in time,
daughter, I was so thirsty.

827
01:48:48,440 --> 01:48:51,320
- Enjoy your drink, father.
- Thank you.

828
01:48:51,750 --> 01:48:55,620
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of
Allah, the Most Beneficent, the Most Merciful.)

829
01:48:56,010 --> 01:48:57,460
Thank you.

830
01:49:10,070 --> 01:49:16,070
Now that their game is exposed,
they can no longer blame Osman.

831
01:49:21,170 --> 01:49:22,700
Uncle.

832
01:49:23,240 --> 01:49:26,700
We want to do business,
trades with these men but...

833
01:49:27,330 --> 01:49:31,070
... I say this castle is
boiling like a cauldron.

834
01:49:31,230 --> 01:49:36,870
First, the assassination of the governor,
now that man called Theokoles.

835
01:49:37,950 --> 01:49:41,620
It seems there is a big conflict
behind those stone walls.

836
01:49:44,570 --> 01:49:49,760
That's better, my nephew,
the more that place boils...

837
01:49:50,170 --> 01:49:53,380
... the more we benefit from it.

838
01:49:58,030 --> 01:50:02,030
You are talking nicely,
that's good, but...

839
01:50:02,930 --> 01:50:06,930
... what if Osman is not
as innocent as we think?

840
01:50:25,000 --> 01:50:29,000
- What about Dündar Bey and Batur, my Bey?
- They will all pay for this!

841
01:50:46,800 --> 01:50:49,460
Sergeant Samsa, you can stop now.

842
01:50:49,930 --> 01:50:53,670
Don't worry, we are with Osman Bey.

843
01:52:18,100 --> 01:52:22,040
- You look so happy Bala Hatun.
- My Alaca is here.

844
01:52:22,220 --> 01:52:24,020
How is Alaca now?

845
01:52:24,890 --> 01:52:28,890
It seems Osman Bey healed your
horse, since you are so happy.

846
01:52:29,270 --> 01:52:33,270
I don't know if his hands are blessed,
he healed my horse in one night.

847
01:52:33,540 --> 01:52:37,270
I don't know if his hands are blessed,
but...

848
01:52:37,490 --> 01:52:41,880
... he is surely feeling something if
he brought it back in one night.

849
01:52:44,060 --> 01:52:48,040
What are you trying to tell, Gonca Hatun?
Don't hold yourself.

850
01:52:48,110 --> 01:52:52,860
I asked the customers coming from Kayı,
Osman Bey doesn't have a wife.

851
01:53:00,550 --> 01:53:04,550
A brave man like him always has a lover.

852
01:53:05,440 --> 01:53:09,590
I asked about it thoroughly,
he doesn't have a lover either.

853
01:53:14,080 --> 01:53:18,460
And why are you telling
me all this, Gonca Hatun?

854
01:53:18,530 --> 01:53:21,720
I saw how he looked at you at the stall.

855
01:53:22,470 --> 01:53:27,420
Aslı and Kerem, you did a
great job, it's beautiful, but...

856
01:53:27,900 --> 01:53:32,550
... It's not just the porcelain,
your horse's treatment is also done.

857
01:53:44,830 --> 01:53:48,610
He jumped into the danger for Aygül
Hatun without a second thought.

858
01:53:49,410 --> 01:53:53,010
She's his uncle's daughter,
what would've he done?

859
01:53:53,920 --> 01:53:56,500
He wouldn't let her die, would he?

860
01:53:57,300 --> 01:54:01,780
And, would that be an action worthy
of a famous man like Osman?

861
01:54:05,320 --> 01:54:06,930
Are you jealous?

862
01:54:15,550 --> 01:54:17,950
Put these jugs on the stalls.

863
01:54:18,800 --> 01:54:23,080
- And take a look at the empty stalls.
- Don't be stubborn, Bala Hatun.

864
01:54:23,720 --> 01:54:28,700
I can take a look at the stalls,
but you should take a look at your heart.

865
01:56:26,010 --> 01:56:29,760
- Good day to you, sisters.
- Good day to you too.

866
01:56:29,980 --> 01:56:31,670
- Welcome.
- Thank you, lady.

867
01:56:32,190 --> 01:56:35,810
There's a white horse in the
stable, they said it was yours.

868
01:56:36,290 --> 01:56:39,380
- What happened to my Alaca?
- He was restless all of a sudden...

869
01:56:39,410 --> 01:56:42,400
... now he is dying. You should
come and take a look, sister.

870
01:56:43,430 --> 01:56:46,670
- I'm going there Gonca.
- Okay, Bala Hatun.

871
01:57:05,050 --> 01:57:08,300
- Can you watch over the stall?
- Don't worry, sister.

872
01:57:39,280 --> 01:57:40,500
I'm here sister!

873
01:58:21,790 --> 01:58:23,930
You are so beautiful.

874
01:58:24,600 --> 01:58:26,340
It's such a pity.

875
01:58:34,500 --> 01:58:36,070
Take her!

876
01:58:37,870 --> 01:58:41,870
Attack the market,
kill everyone! Go!

877
02:00:14,790 --> 02:00:16,410
Welcome, Osman Bey!

878
02:01:59,170 --> 02:02:03,510
You won't be able to
get away with this, Osman.

879
02:02:03,800 --> 02:02:06,490
There's no excuse for foulness...

880
02:02:06,700 --> 02:02:09,140
... and no relief from treachery.

881
02:02:20,340 --> 02:02:22,170
What are you doing, my Bey?

882
02:02:46,020 --> 02:02:49,400
You are still a foul one, my uncle's son.

883
02:03:01,250 --> 02:03:02,190
Now!

884
02:03:03,640 --> 02:03:05,410
Listen to me carefully!

885
02:03:09,770 --> 02:03:13,770
Whoever causes unrest, become a traitor...

886
02:03:14,750 --> 02:03:19,150
... whoever tries to play foul
games behind my back...

887
02:03:20,260 --> 02:03:21,240
... I...

888
02:03:22,500 --> 02:03:25,850
Osman, son of Ertuğrul Gazi...

889
02:03:27,340 --> 02:03:30,490
... swear on the holy
hide my father sat on...

890
02:03:31,270 --> 02:03:34,770
... and on the banner
which we live under...

891
02:03:35,200 --> 02:03:36,120
... and...

892
02:03:36,710 --> 02:03:41,670
... on my black sword
that I carry on my belt...

893
02:03:42,060 --> 02:03:43,660
... I won't have mercy!

894
02:03:46,600 --> 02:03:50,880
I will swallow like a flood,
I will burn like fire!

895
02:03:54,610 --> 02:03:57,740
I will cut the ears that
don't listen to my warnings...

896
02:03:59,400 --> 02:04:03,320
... and the tongues that say
anything else on my words!

897
02:04:07,740 --> 02:04:13,380
Let it be known, and be said like this!

898
02:04:14,060 --> 02:05:08,350
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com